WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.870
- Today is the first
January of the new year

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.830
so, first of all, happy
new year to everyone

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.640
and welcome to this new
video on Firm Learning.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.600
Today, I want to talk about goal-setting

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.070
on how to set goals for the new year

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.100
because I know that at the end of one year

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.490
at the start of the new,

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.600
everyone thinks about,
"What are my priorities?

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.820
What are my resolutions?

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.940
What do I want to achieve
in the next year?"

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.090
And surely this is also
what I am doing for myself

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.580
and when I set goals for myself,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.500
I like to use the methodology of OKRs-

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.560
objectives and key results.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.000
This is the methodology
that was first described

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.050
by Andy Grove, the legendary CEO of Intel,

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.480
also described in his book,
"High Output Management,"

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.880
that I will link also below in
case you're interested in it.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.640
And it's a methodology
that got implemented

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.760
by most of the tech companies out there

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.710
and also more and more of
the old-economy companies

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.434
are rolling the OKR framework out as well.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.200
OKR stands for objectives and key results.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.760
The idea is that you do define

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.130
an objective that you want to achieve

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.370
but then also back it up
with some key results-

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.920
things that you want to see,
that you want to accomplish,

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.100
that then load into the
objective that you want to reach.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.550
When I like to set my goals,

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.430
I like to cluster them
in three different areas.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.380
The first is professional goals,

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.640
second sports and health goals,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.700
and then third also personal growth goals.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.680
So, I will now show you exactly how

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.430
I approach this goal-setting
for the new year-

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.960
what the things are that
I want to accomplish

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.090
in the next year.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.070
And I do hope that this
serves as a motivation for you

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.130
as well for the goals that
you might set for yourself.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.980
So, without further
ado, let's get into it.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.480
This is my goal-setting sheet

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.660
and you see the three areas
that I set my goals in,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.760
but let's start with
the professional goals.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.790
And as some of you know,

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.600
I work for Munich-based proptech company

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.030
called Building Radar.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.657
Of course, I have many goals
